<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">French Fifth Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1958 CE – present · capital Paris</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The present French state, founded by de Gaulle in 1958 with a strong presidency, which ended the Algerian War and helped build the European Union.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Algerian crisis of 1958 brought down the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-fourth-republic">French Fourth Republic</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a> returned to power and a new constitution, approved by referendum in September 1958, created a powerful presidency alongside a parliament. De Gaulle became the first president in January 1959.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">De Gaulle</a> ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algerian-war">Algerian War</a> with Algerian independence in 1962, introduced direct election of the president that year, built an independent nuclear deterrent and left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO's</a> integrated command in 1966. The May 1968 protests shook the regime. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-mitterrand">François Mitterrand's</a> election in 1981 brought the left to power, and periods of cohabitation followed.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> remains a secular republic at the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>, using the euro since 1999. A 2000 reform cut the presidential term to five years. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emmanuel-macron">Emmanuel Macron</a> was elected president in 2017 and re-elected in 2022.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/french-fifth-republic.jpg" alt="French Fifth Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown Vector: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1958 CE – present</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Paris</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Charles de Gaulle, François Mitterrand, Emmanuel Macron</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>France, French Republic</dd></dl></aside></div>
